28. ADMIN PANEL INTEGRATION

The User Panel and Admin Panel must share a consistent Firebase data model.

When an authorized administrator publishes a movie:
• The movie becomes available in the appropriate User Panel sections.
• Its category is respected.
• Its publication status is respected.
• Its featured/trending configuration is respected.
• Its membership restrictions are respected.

When an administrator updates metadata:
• The User Panel reflects the update through real-time listeners or a suitable refresh strategy.

When an administrator unpublishes content:
• It must no longer appear in public catalogue queries.
• Existing references must handle the unavailable state.
• Access to restricted streams must be denied by the trusted access-control system.

When an administrator deletes content:
• The User Panel must not crash.
• Broken references must be handled gracefully.
• Related user history should be retained or cleaned up according to policy.

Do not create a separate hardcoded content database inside the User Panel.

Use shared collection names and field definitions.

If the Admin Panel already uses a different schema, document and implement an explicit mapping instead of silently creating an incompatible schema.

