30. REAL-TIME SYNCHRONIZATION

Use Firestore onSnapshot for suitable real-time catalogue and configuration updates.

Use Realtime Database only where it is appropriate and configured.

Do not duplicate the same content in Firestore and Realtime Database without a documented reason.

Real-time updates should cover:
• Published content
• Hero slides
• Home sections
• Categories
• Membership plan display
• Public announcements
• User notifications
• User profile updates where appropriate

Requirements:
• Clean up listeners.
• Avoid duplicate subscriptions.
• Handle permission errors.
• Handle offline state.
• Avoid unbounded listeners.
• Use query constraints.
• Do not assume Security Rules filter query results.

IMPORTANT FIRESTORE RULE:
Firestore Security Rules are not filters.

If public users may read only published movies, the client query must match the authorization model.

For example, public catalogue queries should constrain the relevant publication fields.

Handle documents with missing or legacy fields carefully.

Do not solve query permission errors by opening every collection to public reads.

